      en: ["Mount Sandel Mesolithic site dates back over 9,000 years.", "Coleraine was the first county town of County Coleraine (now Londonderry).", "The University of Ulster at Coleraine was Northern Ireland's second university.", "The town's name in Irish, Cúil Raithin, translates to 'nook of ferns'.", "The River Bann flows from Lough Neagh to the Atlantic Ocean at Barmouth.", "St. Patrick is said to have founded a church in Coleraine in the 5th century."],
