      en: ["The Irish name 'Bun an Phobail' translates to 'foot of the parish'.", "A high cross at Cooley near Moville dates to the early Christian period.", "Moville was a major port of call for the Anchor Line of steamships in the 1800s.", "Field Marshal Montgomery had strong family ties to the local area.", "Moville Green is among the largest designated seaside greens in Ireland.", "The population was recorded at approximately 1,481 in the 2016 census."],
